<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants — Code-to-model traceability: 74/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Nearly every modelling function carries an equation or figure pointer (Eq. 3.12, 4.9, 4.14-4.16, 5.14, 5.15, section 4a, 2002 section 1.1, Figs. 16-17, 29-36, 37-40), the section-2b comment states the amplitude equations being solved, and upstream artefacts (m <= 4 truncation, +-1.5 clamp, 10-harmonic sum) are labelled as such with their planform.rs lines. Deductions: (a) -8 because the central new step, the Q term with its 3 s_3 and 2 s_2^2 prefactors and the two resolvent insertions at K = k_i +- k_j, is tied to no specific equation of the paper (\"derived here for the operator as implemented\"); (b) -6 because the ledger hard-codes the explanation \"=> 2k harmonic of tanh o max\" while the numbers it prints (0.97/1.00/ 0.17) show the sqrt(3)k ring dominating; (c) -5 because the 0.5 and (-1)^n factors in lateral_weight_coeff, the sharpness/tanh rendering nonlinearity and sigma0 = 1/2 as \"the paper's case\" are asserted without a reference; (d) -4 for stale in-code comments (line 2429: \"/3.1 so q* ~ 4.5 and lambda_c ~ 2.8 mm\" versus the preset's /3.3, 4.84, 2.60 mm) and the false \"< 1 degree\" quantisation claim; (e) -3 because the docstring's \"exact two-regime map\" paragraph still describes the exact map as the pullback used, whereas the default is now conformal." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-code-traceability-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-code-traceability-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-code-traceability-4> ;
    pk:hasScore 7.4e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants — Model fidelity to source: 74/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Verified against the papers: the local harmonics W_n = e^{-2n^2 xi^2} - A e^{-2n^2 xihat^2}, the lateral Fourier-Bessel harmonics (-1)^n e^{-x} I_n(x) with x = xi^2 q^2/4 and the sin(2n theta0)/(2n theta0) spread factor, the O(beta^2) dispersion lambda_+- = W_1 + beta(W_0 +- W_2) + ..., the 2001 Eq. 2.1 map with the paper's w0 = 0.087 and eps = 0.051, the sigmoid ratios s_2 = (1-2 sigma0)/2 and s_3 = (6 sigma0(1-sigma0)-1)/6, and the standard Lambda_r = eta^2 gamma0/(2 gamma_hex - gamma0)^2 < Lambda_h thresholds are all correct, and the m=0/m=1 regime is read off the exact operator's top eigenvector rather than imposed (the fixture presets that impose it are flagged). Deductions: (a) -8 because the quadratic- feedback term Q and its 3 s_3 / 2 s_2^2 prefactors are \"derived here for the operator as implemented\", not pinned to Eq. 5.15, and in the derived m=0 regime the path is subcritical/near-resonant at every sigma0 != 1/2 (my sweep 0.3-0.7 gave roll margins of -105 to -117 and SUBCRITICAL at 4/5 points), so the new physics is untestable where the gallery lives; (b) -6 because the rendered hexagonal planform has wavevectors at 0, +-114.6 deg (n_y = 10 of 11 cycles), a 5.4 deg distortion that contradicts the \"< 1 degree\" docstring claim, so the badged 60-deg hexagon is not what is drawn; (c) -5 because the 1e-15 \"parity\" is with the MesmerPrism Rust port, no paper curve (Figs. 16-17, 37-40) is digitised and compared, and alpha, beta come from that port; (d) -4 because the parity presets sit 3.2x off the paper's wavelength and the paper-scale preset is an ad hoc 1/3.3 rescaling of the lateral widths; (e) -3 because the perturbative n=1 q* (1.491) is still what the CSV calls critical_q for the m=0 gallery rows that are actually rendered at q_mode = 1.404." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-model-fidelity-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-model-fidelity-4> ;
    pk:hasScore 7.4e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants — Morphometric validation: 58/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Quantities are computed on the output and compared with numbers from the literature: ring counts fovea -> 90 deg versus the paper's 30-36 perceived stripes, lambda_c versus 2.4-3.2 mm, foveal magnification versus 11.5 mm/deg, the map's M(E) versus Horton & Hoyt (1991) over 1-40 deg (RMS 6.8%), plus internal FFT k*, spoke counts, spiral pitch, chirality and seam metrics, and the disagreements are printed rather than tuned away. Deductions: (a) -14 because the reference values are the paper's own summary statements and a magnification law, not measurements on hallucination/phosphene specimens (no Kluever/Siegel spiral pitch, no ring-spacing data, nothing from Rule 2011's psychophysics is compared to a model-derived quantity); (b) -10 because the gallery presets fail the one perceptual criterion they are compared to (9.0 vs 2.4-3.2 mm; 8.4 rings vs 30-36) and only the ad hoc paper-scale preset reaches it, and only on the Horton & Hoyt map (32.2) not on the model's own map (29.0); (c) -8 because the honeycomb/cobweb/rhombic panels have no morphometric compared to anything (cell size, spoke count 0.0 reported but unreferenced); (d) -5 because spiral pitch is validated against the requested angle (self-consistency), and the H&H comparison hides a 30% max error and E2 = 1.71 vs 0.75 deg behind the RMS figure; (e) -5 because the Floquet panel reports only the fixture's RMS, no quantity of this model." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-measurement-bressloff-v1-form-constants-stability-reports-parity-max>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-measurement-critical-branch-parity-flips-over-the-lateral-spread-sweep-0-90>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-measurement-exact-orientation-operator-m-8-vs-perturbative-n-1-scan-at-fig17-c>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-measurement-full-cubic-roll-stability-margin-min-2-0-1-in-the-derived-non-contoured-regime-gallery-tunnel>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-measurement-gallery-panels-whose-rendered-lattice-is-the-branch-the-full-cubic-amplitude-equations-select-rhombic-angle-free>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-measurement-gaussian-only-negative-control-critical-wavenumber-q-lateral-inhibition-0>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-measurement-kl-ver-honeycomb-hex-linear-cortical-planform-spectral-ring-wavenumber-k>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-measurement-kl-ver-tunnel-rings-cortical-planform-spectral-ring-sharpness-derived-non-contoured-roll>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-measurement-local-inhibition-threshold-a-loc-at-which-the-critical-harmonic-switches-m-0-m-1-w-w>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-measurement-mexican-hat-lateral-inhibition-critical-wavenumber-q-bressloff-2001-fig-16>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-measurement-paper-scale-preset-paper-scale-tunnel-lateral-widths-3-3-critical-cortical-wavelength-c>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-measurement-preset-runs-reproduced-with-exact-parity-paper-calibration-json-runs>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-measurement-regime-map-cells-a-loc-where-the-cubic-truncation-is-unreliable-subcritical-or-feedback-dominated>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-measurement-rendered-cortical-wavelength-c-relative-to-the-paper-s-stated-2-4-3-2-mm-parity-preset-lateral-widths>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-measurement-retino-cortical-magnification-vs-horton-hoyt-1991-rms-relative-error-over-1-40-deg>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-measurement-rule-et-al-2011-fig-8-overlay-domain-normalised-rms-error-diagnostic-no-calibration-claim>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-measurement-spiral-retinal-pullback-chirality-1-max-r-lr-r-ud-conformal-map-full-field>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-measurement-spiral-retinal-pullback-seam-contrast-conformal-angular-map-rendered-default>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-measurement-upstream-fixture-paper-expectation-checks-passed-paper-calibration-json-stability-reports-runs>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-morphometric-validation-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-morphometric-validation-2>,
